You don't say anything about the VMS form you are using to print to this 
printer. Have you made sure that it's width has kept up with your terminal 
width and doesn't have something fun like 'truncate' as an attribute on the 
form?

Are you using anything special to print to the printer, like DECprint or 
another product? You may need to check there if you are. 

Lastly, you might try setting the term port to be NOFORM. Sometimes this is a 
magic incantation.

Hope some of this helps...

